---
description: Never show undefined/null/NaN in user-facing UI text
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Undefined in UI Copy

Never let `undefined`, `null`, or `NaN` appear in user-visible strings (labels, status, progress, captions, errors).

- Coerce API/progress numbers with a finite fallback before interpolating (e.g. `asNumber(v, 0)`).
- Build labels from validated parts; do not use raw template strings like `` `${done}/${total}` `` when fields may be missing.
- Prefer sending zero values in JSON for progress fields (`done`, `total`, `percent`) instead of omitting them with `omitempty`.
- If a value is missing, show a clear fallback ("Converting…", "0", omit the detail) — never the words `undefined`, `null`, or `NaN`.
